' #FISSURE-PLUGIN 1
' #NAME "Git VCS Adapter"
' #TYPE VCS
' #REQUIRES PROCESS.EXEC
'
' RFC section 15: "Git support should be first-class through an ArcoBASIC VCS adapter, but Fissure
' must not depend on Git conceptually." This adapter is the whole of that dependency -- the native
' core never shells to git itself (see fissure/core/vm/vm.cpp's own comment on FISSURE.Process.Exec:
' there is no separate native FISSURE.VCS.* contract). If the target directory isn't a git
' repository at all (or git isn't installed), DetectChanges reports zero changes rather than
' failing the whole run -- a project may use a different VCS, or none, and the rest of Fissure
' (declared probe associations, the generic file graph) still works without one.

FUNCTION DetectChanges()
    since = FISSURE.Change.SinceRef()
    IF since == "" THEN since = "HEAD"

    result = FISSURE.Process.Exec("git diff --name-only " + since + " 2>/dev/null")
    ' `!`, not `NOT` -- NOT/BITNOT in ArcoBASIC is a bitwise complement, not logical negation (see
    ' [[project_arcobasic_not_bitwise_footgun]] / docs/ARCADE_PROGRESS.md's Session 2 entry in the
    ' main arcobasic repo). `IF NOT result.Ok THEN` would take this branch regardless of Ok's real
    ' value.
    IF !result.Ok THEN
        ' Not a git repo, no commits yet, or git isn't installed -- all legitimate, non-fatal.
        RETURN
    END IF

    lines = String.Lines(result.Output)
    FOR line IN lines
        trimmed = String.Trim(line)
        IF trimmed <> "" THEN ignored = FISSURE.Change.Report(trimmed)
    NEXT

    ' Untracked new files are real disturbances too (a probe could plausibly depend on a file that
    ' didn't exist at the baseline) -- `git diff` alone never lists these.
    untracked = FISSURE.Process.Exec("git ls-files --others --exclude-standard 2>/dev/null")
    IF untracked.Ok THEN
        FOR line IN String.Lines(untracked.Output)
            trimmed = String.Trim(line)
            IF trimmed <> "" THEN ignored = FISSURE.Change.Report(trimmed)
        NEXT
    END IF
END FUNCTION
